/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363969} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bd5fd88-c341-5d33-a06a-b249288d207d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ec437fa-7d05-53d2-8259-19727f28f519" :question/math-academy-id "q-129117" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/037422e7b1ce3b3d9067aba39c4fa85c6311770e63e70758c34aa61629c7f58e.png)\n\nWhich of the following could represent the level curves of the surface $z=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-1,1].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-1,1].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =c \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that the equations $y=-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $x.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-1,1]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of horizontal lines, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cb84bfe-c871-5320-9d4c-83f92579b07b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/7afff53b46a661fc6e0df4df871810dc5514ff7b476294e76c70f60d4e1643f9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363974} {:answer/id #uuid "c637bc28-4d05-5ed2-b6b9-1edf81fd13a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/b79c75fb4de77313ff9ae17938eeabc8b55cca395e6516c09abf6742f9b6a23b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363975} {:answer/id #uuid "dc098fa2-da6b-5025-8d8d-4e55c6bae734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/0162f31b5dbb35c6d370dff9b54257708df39b6957f6547059842cd31769669b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363976} {:answer/id #uuid "bff51616-e5c0-5d20-abc4-71ea33277efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/b4642ea9b585ac066f2ed904b1bee4df7d1ff3449ba2d09afca8364b58f1dcba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363977} {:answer/id #uuid "e067a96f-7163-5e68-ac5f-5ac9b0900d8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/f82efe38e48f39aee18cf9e00cdd69f07c37cc414b08b5bc78ebc0a876c02d7e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cb84bfe-c871-5320-9d4c-83f92579b07b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/7afff53b46a661fc6e0df4df871810dc5514ff7b476294e76c70f60d4e1643f9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363974} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cdebb0d-3dd1-5854-a760-38aa8a17c565" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fdd99af4-5961-5150-ae64-8efce48fac73" :question/math-academy-id "q-129118" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=-x-y+2?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nnotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider $c$-level curves for any real value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ -x-y+2 & =c \\\\ y & =-x+2-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $-1.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/e20175ef9ac473a621a67d524e60cacc6e9a40ba30267fe81b4e6a093c780c28.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a5aba53-12e7-56e3-8c06-c47e6cba8aec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1900/Source/Images/q-35520-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121847} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8e545e-59ab-52bb-92b8-7d108775f54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1900/Source/Images/q-35520-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121848} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f7cccf-e112-58dc-9df7-377dd0485ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1900/Source/Images/q-35520-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121849} {:answer/id #uuid "3add1154-621e-51ad-b5a7-14f1bb2c1088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1900/Source/Images/q-35520-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121850} {:answer/id #uuid "64c445b1-05a4-52ca-8068-63668aba1166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1900/Source/Images/q-35520-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64c445b1-05a4-52ca-8068-63668aba1166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1900/Source/Images/q-35520-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121851} :answer-field/id #uuid "56370a75-a51d-5b32-bfe2-6c3df58783c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f48129ca-8a2b-5a4f-8600-d7fd45c7c512" :question/math-academy-id "q-35520" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of circles centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/413a11a52ed6a4fc76c2848867d664a63fce24dd39088cdd5826b576d8e7b09c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "063c3081-fc99-5c59-9c9c-17dc1247f778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363981} {:answer/id #uuid "e6de069c-00e7-55c3-abef-12f93304c62a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363982} {:answer/id #uuid "93ab8cf8-df3c-545b-9e70-4de71e0b453c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363983} {:answer/id #uuid "40169a3d-04d9-5678-84cf-d8a54ff12072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363984} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e38b30-9540-5800-a818-37d8d43cae7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6de069c-00e7-55c3-abef-12f93304c62a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363982} :answer-field/id #uuid "375cdb08-607e-5f82-98dc-008ebfc21d03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb8b2d04-67d4-51d3-8ebf-71fc804b1a61" :question/math-academy-id "q-35527" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=-1$ gives a parabola\n- $c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=\\pm 1$ then the level curves are $xy=\\pm 1,$ which are hyperbolas.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curves are $xy=0,$ which consists of the axes $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "286957ec-8684-5aae-8c65-4489a40574c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363988} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe6c2e5-9236-5ba4-93ec-d695c3eb9c67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363989} {:answer/id #uuid "97dcfe1e-2ae5-5418-bd47-555110b4615c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363990} {:answer/id #uuid "0c6d9b72-e083-5051-85d3-58f0292d9e58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363991} {:answer/id #uuid "3c88c9de-96bf-5b35-8169-1b8671e4e00d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "286957ec-8684-5aae-8c65-4489a40574c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363988} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba0d035f-188d-5d33-9360-40e5e980a843" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f4b2eba-eaa0-5faa-a68a-66c51bc54701" :question/math-academy-id "q-71395" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives a line\n- $c=2$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=0$ gives two lines" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true."}]}
